WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.030
In Makueni and Machakos
counties, south-east Kenya,

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.410
rain falls in short seasons.

3
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:09.490
After rain, a seasonal river flows.

4
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.510
Much of the rain runs off.

5
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.910
Soon the bed is dry sand.

6
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.830
So a small concrete wall is
built across the riverbed.

7
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.950
Floods drop sand behind it.

8
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.390
In the rainy season, water fills
the gaps between the sand grains.

9
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.970
Why store it there, rather
than in an open pond?

10
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:32.130
In this mission, you'll explore
ways to make water last:

11
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.330
saving, reusing and managing groundwater.

12
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.610
Then you'll see how a sand dam works,
and weigh up the evidence on how well it

13
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.890
delivers.

14
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:46.230
Your mission: explain why villagers in
dry parts of Kenya store water in sand

15
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.880
rather than an open pond.
